  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The ranking lists the top small-business government contractors by contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Total obligations across the ranked firms equal $2.3B. CSI AVIATION, INC obligated $278M, making CSI AVIATION, INC the largest listed small-business contractor for FY2027 to date. SIGNATURE CHOICE III, LLC obligated $226M, THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC obligated $172M, and SALUS WORLDWIDE SOLUTIONS CORP. obligated $150M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC obligated $99.6M, FCN, INC. obligated $91.6M, and MINBURN TECHNOLOGY GROUP, LLC obligated $80.4M. VETERANS DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION, INC. obligated $71.5M, AKIMA INFRASTRUCTURE PROTECTION LLC obligated $69.6M, and SOFTRAMS LLC obligated $59.4M. The note clarifies that all figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial for the fiscal year to date. Use the listed obligations for firm-level comparisons rather than for full-year market sizing because the numbers reflect a partial fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who leads the FY2027 to date rankings?",
        "body": "CSI AVIATION, INC leads the FY2027 to date rankings with obligations of $278M. SIGNATURE CHOICE III, LLC and THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC follow with obligations of $226M and $172M respectively. SALUS WORLDWIDE SOLUTIONS CORP. is next with obligations of $150M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How large are the FY2027 to date obligations overall?",
        "body": "The ranked small-business contractors account for total obligations of $2.3B. The dataset notes that all figures are contract obligations and that current-year totals are partial for the fiscal year to date."
      }
    ]
  },
